# Registry output: every file below is rebuilt from source by `npm run generate -w registry`.
# A feature pull request does not commit it (the `registry (no generated output in PRs)` gate
# fails one that does); the release commit does. So a merge conflict in one of these files can only
# come from the release branch or an old branch, and is never a decision: the `interlace-generated`
# driver keeps this branch's copy (`npm install` registers it), and the next build rewrites it.
# GitHub ignores custom drivers, so its "Update branch" button can still stop on these files for a
# branch that carries them: put them back with the command the gate prints.
apps/registry/public/r/** merge=interlace-generated linguist-generated=true
apps/registry/public/data/** merge=interlace-generated linguist-generated=true
apps/registry/public/.well-known/** merge=interlace-generated linguist-generated=true
apps/registry/public/tokens/** merge=interlace-generated linguist-generated=true
apps/registry/public/llms.txt merge=interlace-generated linguist-generated=true
apps/registry/public/llms-full.txt merge=interlace-generated linguist-generated=true
